    { year: 1984, title: 'DNA fingerprinting', text: 'Alec Jeffreys shows DNA variation can identify individuals; the first criminal conviction on DNA evidence follows in 1988.', tag: 'identification' },
    { year: 1995, title: 'Databases go national', text: 'The UK launches its national DNA database (US CODIS follows in 1998) — cold cases become active investigations.', tag: 'databases' },
    { year: 2009, title: 'The NAS report', text: 'The US National Academies audit the forensic disciplines and call for stronger research foundations — a wake-up still being answered.', tag: 'scrutiny' },
